"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f53c5f4ac01762e934cf358f17814afa64c499678dd029f6c050d2e92ae4d583","event_uuid":"e91997f3-f9e8-42af-9498-17da8975eef2","position":{"commit_sha":"93874931126f4d3f93a7fd2e840356dc9d59f353","position":"1788479829856064581-e91997f3-f9e8-42af-9498-17da8975eef2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8976542d686fbfa624d4a50aba23ac389c735eedcc7e89686d11b28eda90fb01","event_uuid":"19d3a83d-613e-45e0-9b18-7a76390bacd4","position":{"commit_sha":"b6d0c3c7c34cdfcbd609f4cc1605f61c4f27ec50","position":"1788479881733662613-19d3a83d-613e-45e0-9b18-7a76390bacd4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Calibration sample frozen before review.\n\nPopulation: 610 non-archived/visible work tickets of type bug, epic, story, or task whose description length is 7,200–7,999 characters (near) or >=8,000 (over). Excluded session_log and code_review. Selection seed: `20260903-bloat-v1`; rank within each type×band stratum by SHA-256(seed + \":\" + canonical ticket id), then take fixed quotas. Quotas yield 20 unique tickets: five per type and ten per band. This is deterministic preliminary calibration, not prevalence estimation.\n\nShared in all three batches:\n- cibophobic-moist-guineafowl (b928-3ab6-5985-417b), bug, near, 7,855\n- uncheered-sombre-bumblebee (f789-3f9d-8b35-4e0d), story, over, 12,128\n\nBatch A unique:\n- exultant-neofascist-bluegill (1e88-687f-45d1-435f), bug, near, 7,322\n- outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast (0e68-41eb-5782-4336), epic, near, 7,707\n- amenable-befuddling-phoenix (2e0f-e4dc-ee9d-4855), story, near, 7,916\n- coyish-fluent-gibbon (e7a9-35fa-1d58-4095), bug, over, 8,801\n- dissimilar-sorcerous-hartebeest (3393-83ca-5501-4e6e), epic, over, 11,165\n- punctual-scavenger-fallowdeer (2682-b015-4fe5-4066), task, over, 8,379\n\nBatch B unique:\n- camerashy-erectable-frog (301d-0769-ed02-42f6), bug, near, 7,446\n- spin-cub-usher (65dd-e93b-666a-4caa), epic, near, 7,976\n- synonymous-senatorial-cuscus (6e2f-2814-4f92-4873), task, near, 7,965\n- strained-bare-turnstone (df2c-e4b8-496d-4698), bug, over, 10,536\n- elfish-chair-lug (88ab-7052-8850-46d4), epic, over, 18,787\n- enduring-cagophilic-orca (1de3-a19f-c4ea-4b28), story, over, 8,135\n\nBatch C unique:\n- picky-censorable-loon (69e3-748d-0274-45f3), story, near, 7,580\n- sepia-cardiac-hawk (ddcd-fc9e-a81f-4cbb), story, near, 7,243\n- blousy-luxuriant-rasbora (ce7d-3a15-51e5-4c6a), task, near, 7,947\n- jira-reb-1003, epic, over, 10,892\n- stew-kid-motif (6a9a-910a-6938-4695), task, over, 10,393\n- lofty-beech-twang (a118-fa8e-547a-49ba), task, over, 17,211\n\nReviewers will see frozen rule definitions and complete ticket material, but not computed detector firings. They will label overall bloat and each rule's targeted construct as present/absent/not-applicable with evidence and confidence.","timestamp":1788469271058774532},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Calibration complete; full reviewer evidence, per-ticket labels, source links, detector implementation, and recommendations are in session_log 59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148.\n\nThree blind background-agent batches reviewed 24 assignments / 20 unique tickets (two shared): 10 near-limit, 10 over-limit; five each bug/epic/story/task. Adjudicated overall: 6 bloated, 14 appropriate. Shared agreement: cibophobic-moist-guineafowl unanimous appropriate/all rules absent; uncheered-sombre-bumblebee split 1 bloated vs 2 appropriate, with R2/R9 the only per-rule disagreements. Final label: appropriate, medium confidence; dissent retained.\n\nConfusion categories below are count (% of applicable N), with NA excluded:\n\n| Rule | N/NA | TP | FP | FN | TN |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| R1 exact duplication | 20/0 | 1 (5.0%) | 1 (5.0%) | 1 (5.0%) | 17 (85.0%) |\n| R2 near/history duplication | 20/0 | 0 | 0 | 4 (20.0%) | 16 (80.0%) |\n| R3 transcript dump | 20/0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 20 (100%) |\n| R4 empty update | 17/3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 17 (100%) |\n| R5 filler/meta | 20/0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 20 (100%) |\n| R6 sentence/paragraph sprawl | 20/0 | 6 (30.0%) | 14 (70.0%) | 0 | 0 |\n| R7 alternatives/hedges | 20/0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 20 (100%) |\n| R8 imperative saturation | 20/0 | 0 | 0 | 2 (10.0%) | 18 (90.0%) |\n| R9 length envelope | 20/0 | 5 (25.0%) | 13 (65.0%) | 0 | 2 (10.0%) |\n| R10 canonical copying | 19/1 | 0 | 0 | 2 (10.5%) | 17 (89.5%) |\n\nUnion versus overall bloat: TP 6 (30%), FP 14 (70%), FN 0, TN 0; precision 30%, recall 100%, specificity 0%. R6 fired on all 20, so naive OR is unusable. R9 recall was 100% but precision 27.8%; length must remain a review request, not a bloat verdict. R2/R8/R10 require recall work. R3/R4/R5/R7 had no positive controls, so sensitivity remains unknown.\n\nRecommended enforcement: block only objective high-threshold R1 duplication, unsummarized high-volume R3 transcript dumps, and R4 empty updates; keep all other rules advisory with matched spans, protected-fact safeguards, reasoned suppression, and no automatic deletion. Use R6 only for span-level coaching, R9 only with another independent redundancy signal, revision-aware/linked-ticket comparison for R10, and never combine all findings with OR.\n\nLimitations: long-ticket enrichment, 20 unique records, only two triply reviewed records, single reviewer for 18, local current-revision source comparison, and no positives for four rules. Next step is an ordinary-length + positive-control development set followed by a frozen held-out validation set.","timestamp":1788471390440917795},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction completed and independently recomputed.\n\n- R1–R10 are withdrawn as refuted production signals: R1 had FP=TP; R6/R9 had FP>TP; the rest had TP=0.\n- Artifact-scoped guidance now distinguishes executable tickets, comments/handoffs, ADRs, user-facing docs, reference/API docs, incident/security records, and session logs.\n- The fresh-agent check is now: current state, chosen path, constraints, proof, blocker, exact next action (no owner).\n- Three retrospective ticket-only candidates meet the historical admission bar: S1 revision residue TP/FP/FN/TN=3/0/3/14; S2 cross-section echo saturation=2/0/4/14; S3 truncated acceptance residue=1/0/5/14. Their OR is 6/0/0/14.\n- An independent reviewer re-fetched all 20 tickets through MCP and reproduced every fire. The perfect union is explicitly labeled resubstitution, not held-out validation; batch-local candidates had no TP outside their discovery batches, so none is approved for production enforcement.\n- Full definitions, artifact contracts, sources, limitations, and the required held-out/rewrite-effect gate are in session_log 59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148. No repository files changed.","timestamp":1788478715820014909},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close checkpoint: completion verification passed, but close refused with `stale-store` because this MCP clone reports 20 unpushed ticket commits after `final-push-rejected`. No force override will be used. Retrying normal rebar delivery/reconciliation before the close.","timestamp":1788479262863379252}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788468460796481096,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"eb75fefc-79ec-4c78-a3ce-5158e38cf717","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ee0c-1d25-1652-43c3"},{"link_uuid":"dccd3b69-401f-4209-a4fd-62f2619bc138","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nRevise the completed verbosity research after user correction. The original ten deterministic signals were not merely unvalidated: the historical calibration refuted them as production recommendations. The final guidance must be artifact-specific, and any replacement deterministic rule or LLM criterion must show a positive effect on the historical ticket corpus before recommendation.\n\n## Approach\n- Scope writing guidance separately for executable ticket descriptions/plans, ticket comments/handoffs, ADRs, user-facing documentation, reference/API documentation, incident/security records, and session logs/research notes.\n- Treat unchosen alternatives as inappropriate in an executable ticket once a path is chosen, but retain considered alternatives and decision rationale in an ADR.\n- Give user-facing documentation its own contract for task-oriented explanation, examples, troubleshooting, and progressive disclosure.\n- Remove “owner” from the fresh-agent resumption check; test only current state, chosen path, constraints, proof, blocker, and exact next action.\n- Explicitly classify all ten calibration-v1 rules as refuted for production use. Do not describe zero-positive results as useful signals, and do not recommend any signal with false positives greater than or equal to true positives.\n- Mine the frozen 20-ticket sample for new, precisely defined candidate signals. Compute TP/FP/FN/TN for each candidate against the existing adjudicated labels. Recommend only candidates with TP > 0 and TP > FP, while clearly distinguishing retrospective discovery from held-out validation.\n- Record the correction, artifact-scoped guidance, candidate definitions, measurements, limitations, and next validation requirements in the linked session_log.\n\n## Artifacts\n- Updated research in session_log 59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148.\n- Updated calibration findings and final answer.\n- No repository files.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Guidance has separate named sections for all seven artifact classes listed in the Approach.\n- [x] The executable-ticket section excludes unchosen alternatives after selection.\n- [x] The ADR section requires considered alternatives and the reason for rejection.\n- [x] The user-facing-documentation section covers task explanation, examples, troubleshooting, and progressive disclosure.\n- [x] “Owner” is absent from the fresh-agent resumption check.\n- [x] The result identifies each of R1–R10 as refuted for production use and withdraws it.\n- [x] Each newly proposed signal states an executable detector definition.\n- [x] Each newly proposed signal reports TP, FP, FN, and TN on the frozen 20-ticket corpus.\n- [x] Each newly proposed signal has TP > 0 and TP > FP on that corpus.\n- [x] The result labels same-sample findings “retrospective discovery,” not held-out validation or an enforcement basis.\n- [x] The result specifies the held-out validation required before production use.\n- [x] Session log 59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148 contains the corrected research and is named in the artifact list.\n- [x] Repository-file diff remains empty for this task.\n\n## Verification\nRe-run candidate detectors over the frozen 20-ticket corpus, independently check the resulting contingency tables against adjudicated labels, inspect the updated session_log, and report only candidates meeting the empirical admission bar.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1788476259657311347,"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Read-only ticket-history calibration; findings and evidence live in rebar ticket comments and a linked session_log.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e91997f3-f9e8-42af-949